<title>SWITZERLAND: Los Angeles air cargo grows 10.3 pct in May-ACI.</title>
<headline>Los Angeles air cargo grows 10.3 pct in May-ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo handled at Los Angeles' two airports grew by 10.3 percent to 193,178 tonnes in May from May 1996, Geneva based Airports Council International (ACI) statistics show.</p>
<p>New York held its place as the top city multi-airport group with its three airports handling 230,319 tonnes of air cargo in May 1997 up 1.5 percent on May 1996.</p>
<p>Milan saw the greatest increase up 14.7 pct to 16,322 tonnes compared to the same period in '96.</p>
<p>Details of ACI's monthly survey of major city multi-airport</p>
